    "result": "Perfect! All 28 tests are now passing. Here's a summary of the fixes I made:\n\n## Changes Made\n\n### 1. Fixed `eval/index.js` - toxicity metric score calculation\n**Issue**: The `runEvaluations` function was passing both outputs and references to all metrics. The `toxicityMetric` function only requires outputs (and an optional `bannedTerms` parameter), so when references were passed as the second argument, they were mistakenly used as banned terms.\n\n**Fix**: Modified `runEvaluations` to check function arity (`metric.length`) and only pass the required number of arguments:\n- Metrics with 1 required parameter (like `toxicityMetric`) receive only outputs\n- Metrics with 2 required parameters (like `exactMatchMetric`) receive both outputs and references\n\n### 2. Fixed `finetune/index.js` - missing named exports\n**Issue**: The test was importing `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export, but it was only available via the default export.\n\n**Fix**: Added a named export statement to re-export `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `DEFAULT_GOVERNANCE_TEMPLATE`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS` from `schema.js`.\n\nAll 28 tests in the frai-core suite are now passing, and both changes preserve all existing public exports.",
